  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building law enforcement capacity and ranger morale to protect uMkhuze Game Reserves black and white rhino populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In order to protect the indigenous black and white rhino populations in uMkhuze Game Reserve in KwaZulu Natal, South Africa, funds will support operating costs and equipment for rangers to conduct daily rhino monitoring and analysis of rhino sightings, anti-poaching patrols and rapid response to security incidents, and provide training courses for first aid and gunshot and trauma wounds, and to support upgrades to ranger camps to provide reliable water and electricity.</narrative>
  </description>
